  wizardObjectiveText: {fileID: 1106366346}
  taskToActivate: {fileID: 1106366336}
  startsTimer: 1
  timerDuration: 180
  dialogueLines:
  - Welcome to the OR Challenge!
  - In this 2nd Challenge, you will learn how the OR Logic Gate works.
  - The OR gate checks two conditions.
  - Unlike the AND gate, the OR gate only needs at least one TRUE condition to produce
    a TRUE result.
  - This means the result will be TRUE if "The first condition is TRUE".
  - '"The second condition is TRUE".'
  - Or "both conditions are TRUE".
  - The result will only be FALSE if both conditions are FALSE.
  - To complete the OR challenge, your task is to find and submit an item that satisfies
    at least one of the conditions.
  - 'You must "Bring me a berry fruit OR a red fruit." And you must put it in the
    basket for confirmation. '
  - Submitting the corrrect fruit will open the OR Gate to proceed to the next challenge.
  - Submitting the wrong item will cause you to lose a heart.
  - Remember, in the OR logic gate only one correct condition is needed to complete
    the challenge.
  - Choose the correct fruit, put it in the basket, and unlock the OR gate to continue
    your journey in the Logic Realm.
  - Good luck, Student! Use your logic to move forward.
  finalDialogueLines: []
  nextSceneName: 
  successLines:
  - Excellent! The Gate is now open.
  failLines:
  - Hmm... Let's see what fruit did you bring.
  - That is the wrong fruit!.
