  wizardObjectiveText: {fileID: 1754788625}
  taskToActivate: {fileID: 1754788624}
  startsTimer: 1
  timerDuration: 300
  dialogueLines:
  - Welcome to the final challenge of Stage 1 Logical Expressions!
  - In this challenge, you will learn how the NOT Logic Gate works.
  - The NOT gate reverses a logical value.
  - If something is FALSE, applying NOT makes it TRUE.
  - In simple terms, NOT means the opposite.
  - To complete this challenge, you must cross the river and reach the other side.
  - You will cross the river by jumping on lily pads.
  - There are two types of lily pads in the river.
  - "Counterclockwise Spinning Lily Pads \u2013 Safe to jump on."
  - "Clockwise Spinning Lily Pads \u2013 NOT Safe."
  - "Static Lily Pads \u2013 Safe to jump on"
  - If you jump on a clockwise spinning lily pad it will spin faster and you will
    fall into the water, and lose a heart.
  - Observe the movement of the lily pads carefully and think logically before jumping.
  - Avoid the NOT safe platforms, cross the river successfully, and reach the other
    side to complete the final challenge of Stage 1.
  - Good luck, Student! Every jump requires logic and timing.
  finalDialogueLines: []
  nextSceneName: 
